ow flex behavior."},{"markdown":"Appearance rows must use logical spacing and separators for RTL mirroring, while the narrow-container rule changes the shared grid to a stacked row and aligns controls at the logical start.","startLine":291,"endLine":291,"text":"Appearance rows must use logical spacing and separators for RTL mirroring, while the narrow-container rule changes the shared grid to a stacked row and aligns controls at the logical start."},{"markdown":"Settings boolean preferences use one accessible controlled switch with consistent motion, sizing, disabled behavior, and switch semantics.","startLine":295,"endLine":295,"text":"Settings boolean preferences use one accessible controlled switch with consistent motion, sizing, disabled behavior, and switch semantics."},{"markdown":"[[src/renderer/src/components/common/Toggle.tsx#Toggle]] exposes `role=\"switch\"` and `aria-checked`, gates the bounce until interaction so initial hydration stays still, and disables keyframes for reduced-motion users. Settings panes pass their existing localized labels and state mutations through `onCheckedChange`.","startLine":297,"endLine":297,"text":"src/renderer/src/components/common/Toggle.tsx#Toggle exposes role=\"switch\" and aria-checked, gates the bounce until interaction so initial hydration stays still, and disables keyframes for reduced-motion users. Settings panes pass their existing localized labels and state mutations through onCheckedChange."},{"markdown":"Fresh chat session ids are provisional until a turn produces output or completes successfully, so provider errors do not create visible recent-session rows.","startLine":301,"endLine":301,"text":"Fresh chat session ids are provisional until a turn produces output or completes successfully, so provider errors do not create visible recent-session rows."},{"markdown":"The main-process transports still send a generated `X-Hermes-Session-Id` on fresh requests to avoid gateway fingerprint collisions, but [[src/main/he